# Normalize line endings to LF on checkout, regardless of platform or local git config.
#
# Without this file, Windows CI runners (core.autocrlf-driven) convert LF -> CRLF for files git
# treats as text, changing their raw bytes. tests/recall/test_identify.py's
# test_frozen_map_is_sha_pinned hardcodes a SHA256 computed from the LF-committed fixture, so a
# CRLF checkout breaks it on every Windows job (recall#877) -- confirmed pre-existing since #873,
# not introduced by any later PR. Swept for other byte/SHA-pinned fixtures: none found (only this
# one test pins a fixture file's raw-byte hash).

* text=auto eol=lf

*.json text eol=lf
*.jsonl text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
